      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose it could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\nThere's also a process problem. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient, and you've said you're not a clinician.\n\n- **If 50 mg was a typo:** Amlodipine is usually started at 2.5\u20135 mg once daily and goes up to 10 mg once daily at most. I can enter one of those doses if the prescriber confirms it.\n- **If 50 mg was intended:** The treating prescriber should enter it, or tell me directly. They should also document why such a high dose is needed.\n\nWho is the prescribing clinician, and what dose do they want?"
      }
